  "body": "Follow-up of #1953 (item 2: behaviour tests do not depend on the look).\n\nSome behaviour tests also pin a size or a colour. A refit that changes a width or an ink breaks them, but the behaviour did not change. Move each look clause to the page's layout test in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/page_layout.rs`, or replace it with a label, role or state query.\n\nTests (inventory comment on #1953):\n- `tests/fixtures_page.rs` `…offers_mark_for_exactly_one_selected_model`: equal button width (`< 3.0`).\n- `tests/gcode_viewer.rs` `the_cursor_line_is_highlighted`: finds the highlight by its fill colour. A selected-row state flag can replace it.\n- `tests/gcode_viewer.rs` `ticking_trace_keeps_the_window_its_size`, `a_line_wider_than_the_viewer_stays_on_one_row`: window size and row height. These are layout; move them to a `layout_window_gcode` test.\n- `tests/tool_icon_wiring.rs` `every_catalog_row_paints…`, `every_picker_item_paints…`: icon centre inside the row.\n- `tests.rs` `every_registry_kind_gets_its_tab_bar`: keeps nodes with `rect().left() >= \"Operation: \".left()`. A subtree query of the Properties pane can replace it.\n- `tests/edge_click_modifiers.rs`, `tests/geo_row_hover.rs`: park the pointer at `pos2(1.0, 1.0)`. Use `anchors::chrome_point`.\n\nDone means: these tests assert no size, colour or fixed point, and the `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` does not go down.\n",
